      { id: 3, question: 'Can a subclass access private fields of its parent class?', options: ['Yes, using this.#field', 'No, private fields are not inherited or accessible in subclasses', 'Only if marked as protected', 'Only through getters'], correctIndex: 1, explanation: 'Private fields are not accessible in subclasses. They are truly confined to the class where they are defined.' }
