      { id: 'structuredclone', title: 'structuredClone Deep Dive', content: '**What is structuredClone?**\n\nstructuredClone() creates a deep copy of a value, supporting complex types like Date, Map, Set, RegExp, and circular references that JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) cannot handle.\n\n**Code Example:**\n```javascript\n// Basic deep clone\nconst original = { a: 1, b: { c: 2 } };\nconst clone = structuredClone(original);\nclone.b.c = 3;\nconsole.log(original.b.c); // 2 — unaffected!\n\n// JSON cannot handle these:\nconst obj = {\n  date: new Date(),\n  regex: /hello/gi,\n  map: new Map([["key", "value"]]),\n  set: new Set([1, 2, 3]),\n  data: new ArrayBuffer(16)\n};\n\n// JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj)) loses type info!\nconst jsonClone = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj));\nconsole.log(jsonClone.date instanceof Date); // false!\nconsole.log(jsonClone.map instanceof Map);   // false!\n\n// structuredClone preserves types!\nconst deepClone = structuredClone(obj);\nconsole.log(deepClone.date instanceof Date); // true!\nconsole.log(deepClone.map instanceof Map);   // true!\n\n// Handles circular references\nconst circular = { name: "root" };\ncircular.self = circular; // Circular!\nconst clonedCircular = structuredClone(circular);\nconsole.log(clonedCircular.self === clonedCircular); // true!\n```\n\n**Cloning Strategies Comparison:**\n```javascript\nconst obj = { a: 1, b: new Date(), c: new Map() };\n\n// 1. Spread (shallow only)\nconst spread = { ...obj };\nspread.b === obj.b; // true — same Date reference!\n\n// 2. JSON (loses types, no circular)\nconst json = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj));\njson.b instanceof Date; // false!\n\n// 3. structuredClone (deep, preserves types)\nconst deep = structuredClone(obj);\ndeep.b instanceof Date; // true!\ndeep.c instanceof Map;  // true!\n```\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Cannot clone functions\n- Cannot clone DOM nodes\n- Cannot clone some custom classes (without structuredClone support)\n- Throws DataCloneError for unsupported types\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n1. structuredClone() creates true deep copies with type preservation\n2. Supports Date, Map, Set, RegExp, ArrayBuffer, and circular references\n3. Use structuredClone() over JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) for complex data' }
