      { id: 'error-cause', title: 'Error Cause Property', content: '**What is the Error Cause Property?**\n\nThe cause property (introduced in ES2022) allows you to chain errors by specifying the original error that caused the current one. This preserves the full error context for debugging.\n\n**Code Example:**\n```javascript\n// Basic usage\ntry {\n  fetchData();\n} catch (error) {\n  throw new Error("Failed to load dashboard", { cause: error });\n}\n\n// Chained errors\nasync function fetchUser(id) {\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch("/api/users/" + id);\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      throw new Error("HTTP " + response.status);\n    }\n    return response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    throw new Error("Failed to fetch user " + id, { cause: error });\n  }\n}\n\nasync function loadDashboard() {\n  try {\n    const user = await fetchUser(1);\n    return user;\n  } catch (error) {\n    throw new Error("Dashboard load failed", { cause: error });\n  }\n}\n\n// Accessing the chain\ntry {\n  await loadDashboard();\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(error.message);       // "Dashboard load failed"\n  console.log(error.cause.message); // "Failed to fetch user 1"\n  console.log(error.cause.cause.message); // "HTTP 404"\n}\n\n// Custom errors with cause\nclass ValidationError extends Error {\n  constructor(message, field, cause) {\n    super(message, { cause });\n    this.name = "ValidationError";\n    this.field = field;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validate(data) {\n  try {\n    parseJSON(data);\n  } catch (error) {\n    throw new ValidationError("Invalid data", "data", error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Error Logging with Cause Chain:**\n```javascript\nfunction logErrorChain(error, depth = 0) {\n  const indent = "  ".repeat(depth);\n  console.log(indent + error.constructor.name + ": " + error.message);\n  if (error.cause) {\n    logErrorChain(error.cause, depth + 1);\n  }\n}\n\ntry {\n  await loadDashboard();\n} catch (error) {\n  logErrorChain(error);\n  // Error: Dashboard load failed\n  //   Error: Failed to fetch user 1\n  //     Error: HTTP 404\n}\n```\n\n**Best Practices:**\n- Always pass the original error as cause when re-throwing\n- Use custom error classes with cause for domain-specific errors\n- Log the full error chain for debugging\n- Check error.cause before accessing it (it can be undefined)\n\n**Key Takeaways:**\n1. The cause property chains errors to preserve context\n2. Pass { cause: originalError } when creating new errors\n3. Always log the full error chain for effective debugging' }
